figdown 0.1 bitfield
# Bit-width overflow: the compact form is the C bit-field convention, so
# an item must fit one `unit`; a field meant to span rows is written in
# the classic form (see 403), which keeps the documented spanning.
bitfield b "Overflow" word=32 numbering=lsb0
field ok:8,wide:40
field "tail" 24
